  TITLE "De Natura Sonorum (1975)  („On the Nature of Sound“)"
  AUTHOR "Bernard Parmegiani (1927 – 2013) "
  <NOTES 3 3
    |Bernard Parmegiani (1927 – 2013) 
    |De Natura Sonorum (1975)  („On the Nature of Sound“)
    |	-> Daraus: II. Accidents / Harmoniques
    |
    |Part I: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lXs4RwvyIWw&list=OLAK5uy_l3-5wTbIm7pQDZ7LQ7HZQtUFDfeuTVaPc
    |Part II: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3WlOcEjnvxA&list=OLAK5uy_l3-5wTbIm7pQDZ7LQ7HZQtUFDfeuTVaPc&index=2
    |
    |-> Aspects of Musique concréte:  an experimental music composition technique that uses recorded real-world or natural sounds as its primary raw material rather than traditional musical notation or live instruments. 
    |
    |https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musique_concr%C3%A8te
    |
    |Acousmatic, adjective: referring to a sound that one hears without seeing the causes behind it.
    |
    |-> Extrapolate the sonic event from its corporal source and therefore free it from its semantics.
